{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/efcore/pulls/38924","id":4447873114,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAPaMMs8AAAABCR0oWg","html_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/efcore/pull/38924","diff_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/efcore/pull/38924.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/efcore/pull/38924.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/efcore/issues/38924","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/efcore/pulls/38924/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/efcore/pulls/38924/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/efcore/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/efcore/issues/38924/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/efcore/statuses/35eaddc87c7a8e179de1c7c1a0b71a9332669db3","number":38924,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"[release/11.0] Fix UPDATE ordering regression for unique-index reassignment","user":{"login":"Copilot","id":198982749,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOC9w8XQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1143301?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/copilot-swe-agent","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixes #38917\r\n\r\n**Description**\r\n`AddUniqueValueEdges` runs two passes over commands sharing a unique index value:\r\n- **Pass 1** registers a command as a predecessor under the value it's *releasing*, skipping `Modified` commands whose original value equals the current value (correct — they aren't releasing anything).\r\n- **Pass 2** matches successor commands against those registered predecessors to add ordering edges. #38581 added the same \"skip if original == current\" check here too. But this check is redundant — pass 1 already guarantees `indexPredecessorsMap` only contains genuine releasers — and unsafe: for an attached entity fixed up via navigation, the original-value snapshot can equal the current value even though the property is genuinely changing. This caused the needed release→acquire edge to be silently dropped, letting the acquiring UPDATE run first and collide with the still-owning row.\r\n\r\n**Customer impact**\r\nException thrown on SaveChanges in the affected cases. A workaround it to always set a different original value, but this isn't always practical.\r\n\r\n**How found**\r\nUser reported on 11.0.0-preview.7\r\n\r\n**Regression**\r\nYes, from 11.0.0-preview.6. It was introduced by PR #38581.\r\n\r\n**Testing**\r\nTests added.\r\n\r\n**Risk**\r\nLow. ","labels":[{"id":1017558838,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMDE3NTU4ODM4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/efcore/labels/Servicing-approved","name":"Servicing-approved","description":"","color":"048708","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":17412816,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAPaMMs4BCbLQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/efcore/milestones/239","html_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/efcore/milestone/239","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/efcore/milestones/239/labels","number":239,"state":"open","title":"11.0-rc2","description":null,"creator":{"login":"dotnet-milestone-bot[bot]","id":286398033,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOERIWUQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9141961?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/user